{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116943","id":3342491888,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7HOmDw","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116943","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116943.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116943.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116943","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116943/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116943/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116943/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/b1cfd8beddeda9788c029eda534cd990548cf78b","number":116943,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"GDScript: Infer typed array results for `Array.map` and `Array.filter`","user":{"login":"zimonitrome","id":17656709,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NjU2NzA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17656709?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome","html_url":"https://github.com/zimonitrome","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #72566.\r\n\r\nChanges typed array inference for higher-order array methods in GDScript and aligns runtime behavior for `map()`.\r\n\r\nThis enables examples like\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar source: Array[int] = [1, 2, 3]\r\nvar filtered := source.filter(func(a): return a > 1)  # Array[int]\r\nvar mapped := source.map(func(a: int) -> float: return float(a) / 2.0)  # Array[float]\r\n```\r\nwhich would previously fail with `Trying to assign an array of type \"Array\" to a variable of type \"Array[int]\".`\r\n\r\n### Commit 1: `GDScript: Infer typed array map/filter results`\r\n\r\n- **Analyzer:** `Array[T].filter(...)` → `Array[T]`, `Array.map(-> R)` → `Array[R]` when callable return type is known. Lambda callables expose resolved signature info via `method_info`.\r\n- **Runtime:** `Array.map()` scans result values to infer a common type and stamps the array. Falls back to untyped when types are mixed.\r\n\r\n### Commit 2: `Core: Add Callable::get_method_info for runtime type introspection`\r\n\r\nReplaces \"value-scanning\" with Callable metadata to get O(1) instead of O(n).\r\n\r\n- **Core:** Adds `Callable::get_method_info()` and `CallableCustom::get_method_info()` virtual. Delegates to `Script` for GDScript/C# methods, `ClassDB` for native methods.\r\n- **GDScript:** `GDScriptLambdaCallable` overrides to expose `GDScriptFunction`'s return type, including script class refs.\r\n- **Runtime:** `Array.map()` reads the callable's declared return type directly instead of scanning values. Deterministic — type comes from the declaration, not the data.\r\n- **Analyzer:** Reads return types directly from lambda/identifier AST nodes when available, falling back to `method_info`. This preserves script-local class identity (e.g. inner classes) that `PropertyInfo` loses.\r\n- **Tests:** Added coverage for native class (`RefCounted`) and custom script class (`Inner`) return types.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI split these into two commits to show both approaches. If the `Callable::get_method_info` API addition (commit 2) is too broad in scope, commit 1 works standalone. Feedback welcome on which direction is preferred!\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097162,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTcxNjI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/discussion","name":"discussion","description":"","color":"ccaaff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-03-02T04:38:24Z","updated_at":"2026-07-10T17:29:04Z","closed_at":"2026-07-10T17:26:58Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"zimonitrome:gdscript-typed-hof-inference","ref":"gdscript-typed-hof-inference","repo":{"id":1170308868,"node_id":"R_kgDORcF_BA","name":"godot","full_name":"zimonitrome/godot","owner":{"login":"zimonitrome","id":17656709,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NjU2NzA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17656709?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zimonitrome","html_url":"https://git